p("siman_004/beit-meir/part-001.txt", "beit-meir", {
  "1#_": `And given — see Beit Shmuel wrote; Rashi also holds this view and this is 34 except preferable to it Torah prohibitions forever and David's decrees; but regarding slave nevertheless they have penalty and convert and freed person permitted with them for they are not literal slaves whose bodies were subjugated to one master — see Chiddushei Ran; further wrote also can say, etc. — doubtful for if so how does he conclude one of those who cohabited with Israelite daughter child fit except per his view that it refers in gentility and in seif 6 begins "they converted."`,

  "5#_": `Child Egyptian — Beit Shmuel wrote; because Ammonit fit and no damage in both and kiddushin and transgression exist — we follow damaged; this is not per what we rule congregation of converts not called congregation and Egyptian permitted with her — no transgression; nevertheless not Egyptian except from generality wherever kiddushin and transgression child follows male — if so difference when convert married Egyptian since kiddushin and transgression child follows male; Tosafot — this does not exist except per his view nevertheless child Egyptian like convert who married mamzeret seif 22; R' Yosei congregation of converts not congregation taught initially "which" to exclude — likewise convert to Egyptian for reason same in both mamzer from nation and Egyptian from them we follow damaged; sugya challenges on Mamar Ravin converts follow damaged if say Egyptian married Ammonit what damage in both — question only on law no damage since not damaged; but certainly even one damaged applies to them as reason of law explained seif 6 in Rashi Yevamot and Tosafot Kiddushin; what Beit Shmuel wrote we rule, etc. — reason only general.`,

  "7#_": `The woman, etc. — child mamzer — see Rema: behold in presumption of mamzer; and since Shulchan Aruch supports and since dispute — safek mamzer; implies per one view definite mamzer permitted with mamzeret; great question: Rema concludes if she says impregnated from gentile trusted to validate child and perforce even gentile also common and how definite mamzer — though lying in claiming impregnated from husband nevertheless perhaps from gentile; must explain presumption of mamzer from concern from husband we hold him definite mamzer and practical difference where entire city Israelites then per one view definite law applies. Chelkat Mechokek wrote: but if woman says husband came, etc. — plain if husband admits appears not safek fit for Shmuel was fit — implies even if known all year in distant land no possibility he came except through name also fit since Shmuel fit; in my view doubtful in substance of Yerushalmi as Rosh said not heard for can say case was among prominent people that night he was with wife before witnesses and Behag brings only proof after we found once so — automatically also this concern included in what said regarding divorcee mamzeret not concerned; Beit Shmuel s.k. 69 in name Rabbi Duran: Rema discusses husband before us and admits did not come — wonder: if so why matter he was abroad even if with her and says did not approach more than twelve months still child mamzer for trusted say not his son and Beit Shmuel emended and wrote Rema discusses when before us and does not say came meaning silent — not in Rema's language; plain discusses when not before us; see siman 144 seif 7 Rema's view to rule even leniency because people do not come secretly; see siman 156 seif 4 — from there no full proof here; nevertheless in my view without safek dispute between Rema and Behag.`,

  "8#_": `Hagahah: woman conceived, etc. — months cause — see Chelkat Mechokek world's difficulty and his answer and Beit Shmuel wrote in siman 37 wrote none and this what he brings there s.k. 5 in name Rema and since brings lower siman complete read maiden until six full years heard practical difference and which days do not help and unlike Chelkat Mechokek who wrote six years of maidenhood suffices with two days and months cause none — Chelkat Mechokek's difficulty in siman 4 can answer one way; who grants I know his resolution; what Maharam challenges in my view nothing for plain Rema in 37 disputes Mahari Minz and rules not like Mahari even in pregnancy as clear in Beit Shmuel itself siman 156 seif 4 in name Rema and from Torah say regarding signs months cause and Chelkat Mechokek came only to resolve Mahari lest stam Gemara not like Mahari; in 37 my opinion not comfortable with his resolution from language no difference between maidenhood and maturity — per his words cannot find side even if brought signs 25 Nisan when reached 1 Elul she is mature; even if strained refers to name six years still question Rema's language sugya Kiddushin regarding father betrothed on road and she betrothed in city saying not on day completes six — per Chelkat Mechokek should say on day begins six; therefore one wishing rely on Mahari's ruling doubtful from betrothal to resolve world's difficulty.`,

  "9#_": `And all gossip after her — see Beit Shmuel; see Baer Heitev; however all this per posekim' ruling; but per Rashi there in Sotah from his language appears he does not explain sugya for prohibition and permission only for elevating marriage — no clarity when only similar and daughter similar to which he inclines more; Gemara challenge and reasoning: marry lekhatchilah stam too — per this explains lekhatchilah when has choice from Torah marry none; proof he explains and this comes from unfit cohabitation — perhaps gentile or mamzer and he explains regarding Israel marrying and for him even if gentile she — we rule fit only that nevertheless lekhatchilah avoid slight unfit; if so went out for her name prostitute not concerned — law regarding prohibition and permission; per his explanation also fine what Tosafot and posekim challenged Shmuel who said marry similar, etc.; how much more what clear in Tosafot Shmuel need not majority cohabitations and concerned even if not very promiscuous for sons — what reason in his words marry kohen even similar because she is drop of fit — what adds Taz regarding safek zona deoraita; see Magen Avraham.`,

  "11#_": `And what Beit Shmuel wrote not like R' Chiya — per his words challenged from this sugya on R' Chiya: how majority cohabitations after husband helps per Mahariyu for kohen; in my view even R' Chiya for practical difference mamzer of sotah for R' Chiya only rabbinic and not only rabbinic safek unlike chalalah for kohen which is Torah prohibition.`,

  "12#_": `And if she is very promiscuous, etc. — see Beit Shmuel wrote; likewise in responsum Mahariyu sugya Sotah discusses in such case truth in siman 24 ruled Rema not concerned even very promiscuous except for kehunah; per Rashi wonders what difference kohen and Israel for mamzer; but siman 88 somewhat explains for daughter to kohen like safek lest prostituted before conceived daughter and daughter chalalah if kohen's wife; nevertheless wonder to establish sugya with Rema's view specifically kohen's wife and contradicts himself siman 24 wrote if husband kohen majority cohabitations not help sons safek chalalim even if not very promiscuous — how possible sugya very promiscuous discusses in such case; more should say per his method therefore not concerned even promiscuous except kehunah and even Israel husband because for kohen even impregnated from gentile daughter damaged for kehunah unlike Israel even gentile impregnated child fit — possible Rema's view per his girsa and if very promiscuous even for sons concerned but per our girsa also sons — no place; already brought Maggid Mishneh wondered on this Maharai in his rulings; in my view his explanation should be silenced and not said; what assisted from Behag in Rosh chapter 17 if so none and never occurred to Behag to explain question in such case — reason plain safek mamzer rabbinic lekhatchilah in question not in such case; strained in Maggid Mishneh wrote and removed to stringency and main law we say, etc. — aroused there are posekim lenient and from this challenge Mahariyu nothing assisted from Behag for his case exempted woman from chalitzah through sons from first wife who was very promiscuous while with him — per his words not similar at all safek zikah Torah law can say Behag admits stringent; he further wrote or general concern lekhatchilah; if so why investigate and derive witnesses since only lekhatchilah concern; also question me: though Rema's explanation thus nevertheless in my view no more than this to exempt without chalitzah where possible; nevertheless Heaven forbid for me to rule after Perishah because in 37 well acknowledged not discussing very promiscuous; I write only to raise very promiscuous in all details — in my view stringent require chalitzah for all posekim; mainly his Rema explanation concerned lekhatchilah and if married not remove; precise since did not write this safek mamzer — nevertheless question how divide regarding congregation prohibition between lekhatchilah and bedi'eved — lekhatchilah too is bedi'eved for regarding shetuki main reliance validate through mother's testimony though Gemara says do not do, etc. — because congregation disqualification always bedi'eved as Maggid Mishneh chapter 18; however on responsum Shevut Yaakov part 2 wrote on Beit Shmuel s.k. 74: lekhatchilah because not voice of ruling because language of R' Yehuda and "do not marry" only lekhatchilah; but Rema and Shulchan Aruch language "and all gossip after her" very difficult explain voice of chapter; if so language concerned for her as zona regarding kohen even Israel married removes; as Shakh plainly also halakhah very promiscuous concerned even for sons bedi'eved — doubtful; for again saw from Tosafot words no proof; for their words in Sotah follow R"T in Yevamot per voice not ceased alone we remove from presumption without witnesses of seclusion; but Rif and Rema even presumption strong for voice not remove without examination; see siman 11 CM s.k. 6 how much more kohen prohibited woman without examination even voice not ceased; if so Shakh's ruling doubtful; see siman 11 Beit Shmuel s.k. 12; however what Beit Shmuel concludes per majority posekim' method, etc. — who are they — what wrote beginning his words and likewise Maggid Mishneh part 15 there found no word except Behag Rosh brings and conversely see Tur explains like Maharam — learn knew father's words also so explains and why not dispute with him — because in Israel no room for this dispute — see there; doubtful; therefore what challenges Taz if so none; but I examined Taz — he claims three reasons: one not similar to R' Gamliel's law and asks since here two majorities to disqualify majority promiscuous before her and majority cohabitations from others; brings proof from R' Yosei's case requiring two majorities to validate — wonder what two majorities here all safek if from husband fit or from others majority; also not plain from Rashi z"l certainly majority cohabitations from others only lest majority from others; whence plain in two majorities to disqualify like majority of city and majority of group she not trusted — conversely Tur siman 6 plain opposite and per Rema's view safek; see there and RaaM's proof from R' Yosei's case more wonder — established like halakhah we rule R' Gamliel when not claiming or claiming lekhatchilah or R' Yehoshua and not halakhah; already ruled lekhatchilah child to be lenient meaning bedi'eved.`,

  "14#_": `Before she was divorced — see Beit Shmuel; and though per Perishah his words strained in Tosafot questioning how bring proof after divorce of first from second when no reason for disqualification from before second divorce from first for appears like gentile since bound for get — and their words in HaChalitz somewhat like Chelkat Mechokek that though per R' Chiya even after second divorce mamzer from first nevertheless should have added they also dispute him here. Nevertheless Beit Shmuel's explanation forced: how possible even after second divorce mamzer from penalty without any reason — if so what difference yevamah who performed yibbum in error where we rule siman 159 since no get from second permitted to first and known sons not mamzerim though transgressed prohibition and not precise — Rosh beginning HaEsh wrote we penalize only if reason lest they say; if so after second divorce what reason to penalize and make sons mamzerim; and for what wrote there in Beit HaBach that Rif's language she forbidden to first forever — because they understand no place for Rav here and reason of prohibition to first not concern lest they say but as clear in sugya there Tanna Kamma and R' Yehuda hold forbidden to first where penalty applies Chachamim made for penalty like willing like unwilling — see siman 15 Beit Shmuel s.k. 73; but what heard from Rav and Shmuel no mamzer from first without reason from Torah to dispute them — for Beit Shmuel no question from what answered mamzer even after first divorce though also no reason — can say per his view since anyway from reason lest they say needed decree get from second why also penalize sons from second while act stands unlike yevamah where not needed penalize with get since no lest they say and act void from outset. However for Rema all spacious for did not decree mamzeret except where appears like gentile and after first divorce even from second not mamzer — see Chelkat Mechokek and Gemara language chapter 9 72b: fine from second mamzer he deduced but 94a implies like Tosafot there and Tosafot wrote not precise this and etc. — question perhaps between safek mamzer and definite but between mamzer and fit precise — nevertheless language implies what teaches and the second is not mamzer means Torah mamzer but rabbinic mamzer; if so in reisha teaches safek mamzer this too Torah permitted — what difference reisha teaches mamzer and in seifa not mamzer and learn teaches precisely; however plain language and the second is not mamzer implies more like Rema — Gemara question possible to strain.`,

  "15#_": `Child mamzer — here must say Beit Shmuel s.k. 30.`,

  "16#_": `Permitted with mamzeret — Beit Shmuel wrote and it seems permitted means etc.; thus Tosafot Gittin 41 proved and in their question thought permitted but from difficulty answered so; and for posekim he brought s.k. 32 mamzeret forbidden with slave not forced and possible therefore wrote and it seems.`,
});

p("siman_004/beit-meir/part-002.txt", "beit-meir", {
  "19#_": `But this was necessary — specifically regarding the child Maharshal was stringent: her trustworthiness applies only because from Torah permitted — and because not plausible to him that mother's presumption should help the child whatever it may be — as mentioned several times in Tosafot; but regarding permitting the woman, even majority promiscuous, he admits trustworthiness per Tosafot' reasoning; therefore regarding trustworthiness for kehunah, though without his reason, nevertheless through definite claim joined with presumption it helps; and it was also possible to strain somewhat and say even Rashba admits this per Maharshal; and what he wrote that in majority promiscuous he is definite mamzer — can say specifically to validate safek with Israelite, as he writes mamzer not safek; even with solid Torah majority permitted; but from what we heard in our rumor we write only for practical difference aliba dihilcheta like R' Elazar that definite mamzer is forbidden — if in majority promiscuous one is permitted only to validate safek with Israelite; practical difference if majority promiscuous in city he is considered definite for mixture in family; and I already wrote this depends on Ritva that R' Elazar does not expound "in congregation certainty" — if in majority promiscuous permitted with mamzeret as definite; joining presumption unnecessary; from Maharshal who ruled Rema's law and wrote learn from shetuki — no proof; per his method indeed true; Tosafot Ketubot 12:42b s.v. hashavtanu — R' Gamliel because woman examines — also divide between validating and disqualifying; possible to strain this presumption even with gentile; question: do women learn law in what forefathers disputed; said per Perishah's view forced; Rashba must strain on second fiancée; wonder Tosafot 14 what Abaye challenges R' Yochanan; nevertheless halakhah strained; some proof for Rashba's method: if per Rema through safek perhaps she went majority void — wonder why distinguish lekhatchilah and bedi'eved between majority promiscuous and majority gentiles; somewhat strained but resolved below Rema's view as clear siman 6 — two majorities only in field; Perishah wrote further; appears posekim did not adopt this view — doubtful.`,

  "20#_": `And know further question on Maharshal above: why needed to forbid — he himself wrote chapter 18 laws of forbidden relations halakhah 41 therefore fetus fit through mother even though ruled do not act etc. — because per his view fetus is bedi'eved; if not disqualified from congregation — if so fine to validate but to permit with mamzeret there is no greater lekhatchilah for he can marry convert — if so how his question because Rema wrote his law in place majority promiscuous and place majority — fine even lekhatchilah like R' Gamliel. Nevertheless question: Rambam explains lekhatchilah need two majorities to validate and specifically in field and this law chapter 15 does not mention except in city and majority promiscuous — and per Maharshal's view since requires two majorities because of lineage and this only regarding Israel certainty not safek and definite mamzer — if so appropriate to rule like R' Gamliel with one majority and this as Tosafot Ketubot who permit shetukim in certainty; but for R' Elazar who forbids and on this we judge — initially no question for Ran plainly lineage concern applies even to safek mamzer — fine and resolves what I wrote Maharshal like Ritva holds R' Elazar does not expound in congregation certainty — however for what I wrote seif 33 per truth automatically for R' Yishmael also certainly elevation in lineage even in shetukim — cannot divide views.`,

  "21#_": `Even if he admits — Beit Shmuel wrote it seems if known she prostituted with fit etc. nevertheless in such case no need two majorities as this language also wrote siman 6 s.k. 31 and there discusses examined well wrote per his method since majority posekim hold one majority suffices and in such case Rema does not dispute; nevertheless not forced; but here question for certainly discusses without examination — if not even with majority promiscuous wonder fit for congregation and how majority gentiles requires two majorities; what plain to him that though known prostituted with fit does not fear lest also prostituted with unfit — and per Beit Yosef's reasoning from rabbinic safek permitted; if so why discusses with majority promiscuous also with majority gentiles — per his view considered majority — strained; Tur can say Rashba's method even safek perhaps she went majority in place; what trusted even majority promiscuous — possible not Beit Shmuel's reason still safek perhaps she went but Tosafot's reason she examines — see Beit Shmuel s.k. 38 for Maharshal's reasoning on Noda BiYehudah.`,

  "27#_": `Hagahah: and he is his son to inherit him — Beit Shmuel wrote and appears even for yibbum we say he is his son; on the early ones I grieve and whence did Nissim Yisraeli learn he inherits from her words when he is not before us (see Piskei Maharai siman 252 wrote likewise and implies from Rosh even if examined mother and said from fiancé impregnated we silence him from properties) — rather he rolls on us that she died without chalitzah and certainly question for we say do not act etc. and no more than this to exempt without chalitzah; appears he relies on what wrote and can say since we judge after him regarding not mamzer cannot divide etc. — meaning fine single woman even if says from so-and-so though lying perhaps child fit from another; but with fiancée once not believed regarding another concerned not from him automatically mamzer and there is disgrace — therefore all considered bedi'eved; likewise Chelkat Mechokek's reasoning — this built on Perishah's words that afterward when she before us and does not claim from gentile no reliance on gentile; but below even with fiancée can divide and say fit from gentile though not on fiancé; and this reasoning as appears in Chelkat Mechokek founded on Ran's explanation in Rashi and appears from his language discusses when method brought in name one who says Chelkat Mechokek chapter 17 wrote in single woman even child considered full lekhatchilah and forbidden even through mother's examinations except with fiancée because of her bedi'eved lest heart be cut — but per what we rule like Tosafot or R' Nachman regarding child even lekhatchilah for her considered bedi'eved — this reasoning not forced at all — doubtful.`,

  "28#_": `Further Beit Shmuel wrote in Perishah etc. — question if she not here safek from gentile and when here and does not claim then from silence admission from Israel and he definite mamzer — if so for Rambam without speech child safek perhaps gentile — see Beit Shmuel s.k. 52; if so even if admits from Israel we rule do not make safek definite mamzer — if so when claims from fiancé though not help validate from father's trustworthiness whence definite mamzer — Beit Shmuel concludes however per what wrote nearby (meaning s.k. 52 and s.k. 53 wrote also Maharai holds do not rely on gentile and makes him definite mamzer) — wonder how thought Tur not concerned for gentile and makes definite mamzer to permit with mamzeret — impossible promiscuous and Israel fenced and from Torah only suspect fit; also s.k. 52 leaves Tur in question and besides this obvious to doubt gentile — also brought proof as in chapter 11 78b one who says this my son mamzer born to me from those liable karet or even both admit — Rashi: father and mother say on fetus in her womb mamzer — not from husband but another man; Gemara: what even per lenient view he does not know if from him impregnated or another — question: fine in reisha says this my son mamzer meaning son born to him from karet offenders can say prostituted with another and not mamzer; but in seifa says not his son because did not cohabit and he mamzer automatically why rely on her superiority knowing more — should say even if says not my son and he mamzer nevertheless not know perhaps gentile — therefore what brought this dispute from change of law Tur wrote and he definite mamzer and Rambam wrote likewise in presumption of mamzer — in my view not worth inventing dispute; proof from law of fiancé though in Rambam itself not said definite mamzer nevertheless not said except presumption of mamzer and if fiancé denied child mamzer — did not descend to distinguish here; and because core law of fiancé as in Gemara Tosafot challenges; and here not admits etc. and here majority promiscuous — all on child and question whence definite majority promiscuous and not majority gentiles (for Perishah fine) — learn discusses city all Israelites and therefore follow majority of city — therefore copied stam this is mamzer from father's testimony as in Gemara and understood in city with gentiles among them safek; and law 19 because spoke on two laws together father says not his son and one who went abroad and there possible concern at time Behag who came through name — and general together likewise presumption of mamzer to note even in father's statements sometimes only presumption safek mamzer i.e. city with gentiles; Tur since separated laws takes here in father's statements definite mamzer for practical difference city all Israelites; and always can say admits from stam rule in gentile and only safek. Maharshal Yevamot chapter 7 siman 11 wrote not clear at all — perforce R' Gamliel's trustworthiness only in definite and perhaps but definite and definite not; and though likewise in Ran in Beit Yosef — in my view no question on Rema not said in definite and definite R' Gamliel admits except where claimant claims definite touching him; but here all agree she definite and world perhaps — trusted; and if because of his denial why care about my definite not on her even one fit witness not trusted to remove presumption.`,
});

p("siman_004/beit-meir/part-003.txt", "beit-meir", {
  "30#_": `Whether majority gentiles or majority Israel — this is safek gentile; if betrothed woman needs safek get — implies even in majority Israel no definite get only safek; if so if after betrothal another cohabited child only safek mamzer; if this safek mixed in widow family if married bedi'eved as siman 2 seif 5 — wonder: from Torah foundling in majority Israel certainly Israel and we say whoever separates — forced in Gemara even because of lineage need two majorities until challenged for one who says temporary ruling from Rav who said but for lineage no — learn Rav's reason for lineage no but because of lineage this Torah complete Israel — how find leniency from this to make from definite mamzer safek; Maharshal chapter 1 Ketubot: if R' Yishmael Israel but for lineage no — Rashi: if daughter forbidden to kehunah; certainly if betrothed woman who is safek betrothed and one who killed not executed on him — reason because some gentiles and some Israelites fixed in city and all fixed whether minority or majority like half-and-half — wonder: certainly from Rashi learn stringently judge him fixed and even in majority gentiles needs safek get — lineage concern applies; but in majority not only safek but fixed complete from Torah as Maharshal himself laws of testimony 28 wrote this language and what wrote here for all he is we do not say in majority Israel to execute on his betrothal — if so regarding lineage we say do not follow majority Israel because of lineage to execute on betrothal — how much more; and already our rabbi explained above betrothal not definite only safek — clear in his words what wrote law 35 reason because fixed — not meaning Torah fixed but because of lineage we consider her fixed — if so question how invent from stringency leniency to make from betrothed definite safek; in Beit Yosef after Maharshal's words in law 35 wrote meaning came to give reason why wrote even in majority gentiles betrothed needs safek get — perhaps his intent per R' Yishmael only needs safek get not definite get for this insufficient gentile or truly in majority gentiles definite get and reason only majority gentiles; Maharshal's language does not teach so from writes and reason because some gentiles etc.; and plainly Rambam law 35 wife of this foundling in province with maidservant or gentile when marries convertess this is safek gentile — Ra'avad and Maharshal challenged learn from Rav as above — see we rule even in majority gentiles only safek get required; though in law 35 possible strain regarding damages likewise what wrote law 35 executed etc. — because said and judge congregation (see Chiddushei Ran Bava Kamma 44b and Tosafot Sanhedrin 78b in pits explained sometimes do not follow majority in money) even in rabbinic safek such not plausible to judge after stringency in lineage not follow them — but to make from definite betrothed or safek mamzer — doubtful; perforce admit understood from Beit Yosef z"l language safek get not precise and not on R' Yishmael but then definite get as clear from Rambam's own ruling regarding saving life majority solid from Torah — and his intent in commentary on mishnah validates them; also found in Magen Avraham general 43 s.k. 36 noticed and what wrote and possible etc.; in my view not possible — examine.`,

  "32#_": `And we uncover the basket over him — Beit Shmuel wrote; and here the infant found presumably the men of the city etc. — perforce what questions Yoma on Shmuel son of Shmuel — behold he did not say we do not follow majority except on remaining fixed; likewise Maharshal in Beit Shmuel wondered — can say challenges per view forced to strain per Rashi that question from half-and-half implies specifically in majority Israel we uncover; but even in half-and-half not; how much more in majority gentiles and one separated — what matter remaining fixed — this no more than half-and-half. However per Maggid Mishneh's explanation in Rambam that Rav who said only to sustain him applies also to half-and-half — if so even Shmuel who said uncover also on half-and-half except in majority gentiles not — this fine even for Shmuel since presumably all moved and no fixed remain — doubtful; and per Beit Shmuel's reasoning not only unnecessary as he wrote but also not plausible — rather they deepened for us Maharshal's reasoning on this law; see siman 60 Tosafot Yehonatan.`,
});

p("siman_004/beit-meir/part-003.txt", "beit-meir", {
  "34#_": `Further Beit Shmuel wrote however question Ran's difficulty etc. — and here court still did not rule on her word — doubtful; after he wrote below discusses even challenger after she testified unlike Perishah — if so can say likewise stam discusses even after court ruled; perhaps this not plausible for then matter has no end; and if living witness testifies this fit and he marries Israelite daughter and again challenger comes on him as mamzer — if trusted, Torah's ways are ways of pleasantness. Further wrote dispute of Taz with Perishah — Ritva on 73 s.v. ika: specifically here they did not remove him from house since hidden so much from eyes they did not rely she would know to recognize which left first; but to say he is not Netin and similar — always trusted as long as no one challenged her — see there.`,

  "35#_": `The safekot — Beit Shmuel wrote Netin forbidden with maidservant; however there they wrote so etc.; but per Rema's view I brought above can say permitted — meaning s.k. 31 wrote in his name mamzer permitted with maidservant because prohibition rabbinic and on mamzer they did not decree for children's enactment — if so can say likewise Netin with maidservant; unlike R"T that maidservant prohibition Torah and mamzer permitted with her because from holiness prohibition — this does not apply to Netin and this is correct; but what wrote except Tosafot' question may Netin marry Netinah — doubtful; meaning for Rema in my view for plainly mamzeret forbidden with slave since no children's enactment with her as he wrote s.k. 32 and clear there in Beit Yosef and Chelkat Mechokek and plainly Netinah forbidden with slave for same reason; Tosafot' question initially not for Rema; if so even what siman 5 end 100:2 and chapter 4 to marry maidservant — can say for Rema permitted — in my view not intent since no enactment for children with her as mamzeret forbidden with slave; though for Rema slave prohibition rabbinic — cannot compare to Netin permission rabbinic.`,
});

p("siman_004/chokhmat-shlomo/part-001.txt", "chokhmat-shlomo", {
  "1#_": `Seif 12: Or his master married him to an Israelite woman, etc. NB see in Beit Yosef who wrote this is only rabbinic; and the difficulty from Gemara see in Peri Chadash Gittin 58 and what he wrote on this in my composition Tashbetz edition 4 YD siman 267 laws of slaves siman 161 — examine.`,
  "2#_": `Seif 14 in hagahah: Woman who conceived from her husband end of Sivan, etc. NB behold regarding woman who immersed 10 Nisan and bore on 2 Kislev and was divorced from her husband — see what I wrote on this in responsum LK Kolmya in siman 13 incidentally in my edition 7 siman 255 — examine.`,
  "3#_": `Seif 19: And if they cohabited with Israelite daughter whether single or married woman child is fit, etc. NB behold whether child needs conversion or not — see in Chemdat Shlomo siman 2 where sages of the generation debated; and in my responsum Mahadura tinyana in hagahot I raised that from Torah needs conversion and for single woman does not need conversion; and in responsum LK Turnfal EH siman 4 in my edition 4 siman 66 I raised that rabbinically needs conversion in every case — see there for it is good; and in my composition Chokhmat HaTorah parashat Emor year 1827; and see what I wrote in responsum LK Tshudnov EH siman 5 in my edition 9 siman 259 — see there with God's help and there I showed faces for both sides; and now seems also to bring proof for both sides; and I will begin — bring proof needs conversion from what is written in Ketubot 44a in mishnah of convertess who converted etc. her conception and birth in holiness — behold she is like Israelite daughter for all matters; and question how ruled and tanna taught behold she is like Israelite daughter for all matters — find also conception and birth in holiness not like Israelite daughter for all matters e.g. if her mother prostituted with gentile — if so though gentile who cohabited with Israelite daughter child fit nevertheless she has no father since child like her — therefore at least no paternal house; and especially reisha from stam discusses born from gentile — true also gentile woman who prostituted with Israelite likewise; but since teaches stam implies discusses stam convertess who bore from gentile — if so from dividing between conception and birth in holiness or not implies one version and also discusses impregnated from gentile — how said behold like Israelite daughter for all matters; and if so should divide in this itself between prostituted from gentile or not — from gentile has (hundred silver) and no paternal house and from Israelite has paternal house; and greater question in Gemara challenges and say conception and birth in holiness and answers that one is elevated Israelite — what answers perhaps teaches even if prostituted from gentile so — perforce proved in such case needs conversion; if so this conception not in holiness and birth in holiness — worse than convertess who converted with her daughter for there her conversion helps also fetus — therefore find conception not in holiness and birth in holiness; but in Israelite daughter who already Israelite then certainly gentile who cohabited with Israelite daughter conception and birth not in holiness since afterward needs conversion — if so we contradict mishnah if conception and birth not in holiness and if in holiness perforce find only from Israelite cohabited — therefore said properly elevated Israelite; this clear proof in my view — examine well; and now I see clear proof opposite does not need conversion — explicit Gemara in mishnah Bekhorot chapter Yesh Bekhor and Gemara 47 and Shulchan Aruch siman 305: gentile who cohabited with Israelite daughter child liable in bekhor redemption as firstborn — if thought needs conversion then convert like minor born and has no brotherhood and kinship and no firstborn — and rather proved in Gemara 47 in what wrote do not say per one who defiles child only even per one who defiles child etc.; and whether per Rashi or Tosafot there proved child disqualified nevertheless does not need conversion since liable redemption — only mamzer; and as written in Gemara Levi called disqualified and if needs conversion not Levi at all — perforce does not need conversion and liable redemption. And behold per what I wrote in edition 4 (cited here) rabbinically needs conversion somewhat resolved — can say since from Torah needs conversion liable bekhor redemption; but at least proved from Torah does not need conversion — examine. And wonder on Shaarei Teshuvah and Chemdat Shlomo speaking this law and did not notice this Gemara — examine.`,
  "4#_": `Seif 26: Single woman who conceived, etc. NB see in my edition YD siman 1 in my compositions siman 95 what wrote there on this law and Beit Shmuel's words in this seif what wrote there with God's help incidentally in responsum to Hungarian community — examine; and see what I wrote at length in siman 13 on nursing woman in responsum LK Botschatsh where I expanded with God's help resolving Rambam's words and resolving Bach's words Beit Shmuel brought here and pilpul in body of sugya Yevamot source of this law — examine.`,
  "5#_": `Seif 27: Fiancée who conceived, etc. and he is his son to inherit him, etc. See Chelkat Mechokek s.k. 28 what wrote in name Bach forbids her afterward to kohen and Chelkat Mechokek wondered on him; see what I wrote in responsum LK Turnfal EH siman 4 edition 4 siman 66 to resolve words of sage Bach brought and I gave reason to distinguish between child and her — examine.`,
  "6#_": `Seif 29: But father who says, etc. trusted to disqualify him, etc. NB behold if he does not say definitely only safek perhaps not his son and likewise if we do not know if majority cohabitations his or not and he claims were not majority his cohabitations and likewise from world but not from many — only from one his law see what I wrote on all this in my responsum Kana Mekoma laws of Ketubot siman 71 edition 6 siman 258 — examine.`,
  "7#_": `Seif 30: One who says about himself, etc. NB see what I wrote explaining Rambam's language on this law in Piskei HaRambam laws 15–16 and all details of this in my responsum LK Bradshan Kana Mekoma laws of Yibbum siman 257 edition 5 siman 122 where I expanded greatly — examine.`,
  "8#_": `Seif 34: If he did not immerse, etc. NB see in Beit Shmuel who brought Tosafot' view regarding damages in majority Israel pay full damage and Maggid Mishneh disputes; see in my composition Mishpat Tzedek on CM siman 1 in my hagahot siman 47 in Mahadura tinyana brought proof from Gemara Shevuot 34 regarding shevuat edim kenas RIH holds exempt — there I proved like Tosafot not their reasoning but since safek did not arise for money matter automatically we follow majority and he is Israelite and extract money through this majority — see clear proof with God's help in such case we follow majority — examine; and in my composition Mili DeNizikin on Bava Kamma 16b I proved there not like Tosafot' reason but even without owner's knowledge do not follow majority in money — see; therefore were it not for our proof in CM above from another reason would appear main law like Maggid Mishneh; but per our proof above main law for ruling like Tosafot not their reasoning — see; and in my composition on Bava Kamma chapter 2 17b we expanded there too and wrote another reason for their law and what to wonder on them — see where we expanded with God's help — examine.`,
});

p("siman_004/rabbi-akiva-eiger/part-001.txt", "rabbi-akiva-eiger", {
  "1#_": `Siman 4 seif 1 mamzerim. NB voice went out on her mamzeret — we are not concerned Gittin chapter 9; and see responsum Maharival part 1 general 2 siman 12 that even with complete voice we are not concerned for regarding this it is like voice after marriage — see there.`,
  "3#_": `Seif 14 but within twelve months. NB and possible they count twelve full months and also give him three more days and hang that seed absorbed on third day — responsum Pri HaEretz to RaaM Mizrachi EH siman 1; and see responsum Orim Gedolim Limmud 110:111 and in Gan HaMelekh to Baal Ganat Vardim letter 158.`,
  "4#_": `In Beit Shmuel letter 19 seemingly difficult. NB see responsum Mahari"t EH siman 15.`,
  "5#_": `Seif 16 that majority of cohabitations we attribute to husband. NB see Maharshal Pesachim chapter 7 in Rashi s.v. viladei zenunim that for elder not majority cohabitations; and see Mishbetzot Zahav introduction 6 collective part 5 letter 25.`,
  "6#_": `Seif 19 child fit. NB and deaf-mute who cohabited with gentile — if we say since no kiddushin also afterward child not mamzer — see Mishbetzot Zahav introduction collective 8 letter 7.`,
  "7#_": `Seif 20 therefore mamzer marries lekhatchilah. NB and even safek mamzer — Radbaz in responsum siman 288; and see responsum Pnei Moshe part 3 siman 1 challenged on this; and see this siman 136.`,
  "9#_": `Siman 25 and with other men. NB meaning they gossiped she prostituted with fiancé also with others; but if not say after betrothal — though say from world before betrothal nothing in this; see responsum Shev HaKohen siman 35.`,
  "10#_": `Seif 29 and if there are sons to the son. NB and if per his testimony he cast aspersion on all his sons — you have sons; or even regarding those without sons — Maharam Padua siman 14.`,
  "11#_": `There hagahah: not trusted except with witnesses. NB see responsum Av Beit HaDin siman 111.`,
  "12#_": `Seif 36 and these safekot have no remedy. NB and that there is no remedy to marry in this — acquire maidservant and free her on condition if I am fit you are freed — then child fit from Torah after release; see responsum Pnei Moshe part 1 siman 1; and see responsum Motzal MeEsh siman 98 raised truth there is remedy in this manner.`,
});

